      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For UK Inheritance Tax (IHT) purposes, UK residents are generally subject to worldwide estate rules, meaning their international assets like Spanish property and US brokerage accounts are included. The value of these non-UK assets is determined in pounds sterling at the time of death for IHT calculation. Spanish property may also be subject to Spanish inheritance tax, so you need to consider both jurisdictions' rules.",
      "source": "target",
